# =====================================================================
#  WHITELIST - nothing goes into the repo by default.
#  Only the pipeline scripts, examples, README and requirements are public.
#  Data, docs, local notes and old versions stay on disk.
#  A new file or folder stays out until it is deliberately let in.
# =====================================================================
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/requirements.txt
!/pipeline/
!/examples/

# --- Still blocked inside the folders that are let in ---
# Python cache and macOS junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
# Stray data: scripts resolve paths from the working directory,
# so a dump can land inside pipeline/ - these rules catch it
*.json
*.jsonl
*.html
# ...except the example outputs, which are published on purpose
# (metadata, headlines and decisions only - no article text)
!/examples/*.json
# Secrets: none of these files exist today, the rules are a safety net
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
KEY*.txt
*secret*